[stderr] 149:## Trust, privacy, and security
[stderr] 150-
[stderr] 151-- Treat content, imported saves, URL parameters, browser events, service-worker
[stderr] 152:  messages, and persisted bytes as untrusted. Validate and bound sizes before
[stderr] 153-  parsing; never execute content as code or render dialogue via unsafe HTML.
[stderr] 154:- Serve production assets over HTTPS with a restrictive content security policy,
[stderr] 155-  no third-party scripts by default, dependency lock/review, and build-time
[stderr] 156-  asset integrity/hash manifest. Do not embed credentials in the client.
[stderr] 157-- Use same-origin storage isolation; minimise persisted data to game state and
[stderr] 158-  chosen preferences. Do not collect names, contact data, precise location,
[stderr] --
[stderr] 162-  purpose, retention, deletion, and transport before collection. A local
[stderr] 163-  diagnostic record excludes free-text dialogue and complete save contents.
[stderr] 164-- There is no authorization role in P0 because there is no server resource or
[stderr] 165-  identity boundary. Locally, a player controls their browser profile; this is
[stderr] 166:  not a security guarantee against a device owner. Any server feature requires
[stderr] 167-  explicit least-privilege roles, authenticated authorization on every request,
